# mytheus-platform / env/prod.db.app.env - the REQUEST-PATH database credential.
# Copy to env/prod.db.app.env and fill. NEVER commit the filled file; gitleaks enforces.
#
# Layered on top of env/prod.env by the `web` and `workflow` services in
# deploy/compose.prod.yml. This file exists so those two processes hold this credential and
# no other: that is the second half of defect D1, where one shared env_file gave every
# process every credential and made splitting the roles pointless.
#
# `mytheus_app` holds neither rolsuper nor rolbypassrls, so every tenant_isolation policy
# applies to it. Never replace this with `postgres` or any superuser "to debug something":
# it disables tenant isolation across the entire product and nothing fails loudly.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://mytheus_app:CHANGE_ME_app_password@postgres:5432/mytheus
